        "uuid": "08a8e35e_1b31afa0",
        "filename": "identity/java/android/security/identity/PresentationSession.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076971
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-04T14:38:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IdentityCredential.createEphemeralKeyPair() would return the same ephemeral key pair the second time it was called on the same instance. \n\nPresentationSession.getEphemeralKeyPair() does the same and I chose \"get\" instead of \"create\" to point out that the key pair is tied to the PresentationSession instance. I\u0027ll add a JavaDoc comment to explicitly call this out. I\u0027ve added \"The ephemeral key pair is tied to the {@link PresentationSession} instance so subsequent calls to this method will return the same key-pair.\"",
      "parentUuid": "705d8d78_b7d070ae",
